  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Superpose a mobile and a reference PDB/mmCIF structure with one US-align global transform, then show which chains correspond, where and how much the structures differ (per-residue displacement, hotspots, 3D patches, gained and lost contacts, rigid-body vs internal motion), and export an auditable result bundle. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
